{"type": "message", "id": "7630c754", "parentId": "6f2afee6", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T07:35:15.782Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_b5b22c04af1843d19e56fa7e", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"2014\\\" \\\"2020\\\" railway suicide Eurostat Germany Belgium Portugal Spain France UK Croatia Bulgaria\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 898,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e75ddc976311c59\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n﻿ | I Report on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU 2020\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e75ddc976311c59\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202020.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fa0c2ac947c788a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFigure A-20: Fatalities per type of accident (EU-28, 2014-18) Figure A-21: Railway suicide and trespasser fatalities (EU-28, 2007-18)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fa0c2ac947c788a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.era.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5631220def7a3e70\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU Statistics Explained\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5631220def7a3e70\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/SEPDF/cache/94376.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2871305905c76004\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt should be noted that there are no railways in the EU countries Cyprus and Malta, ... The number of significant railway accidents in the EU fell almost continuously between 2010 and 2020, with the · only exceptions being <strong>a sharp increase in 2014 (+6.7%)</strong> and a slight increase in 2017 (+2.1%).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2871305905c76004\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51dff60a8f9c4429\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51dff60a8f9c4429\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78b73962f85c0980\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAbstract Background In the European Union, <strong>over 2000 suicides on railway premises were reported in 2020.</strong> Identifying individuals&#x27; behavioral and location patterns just before they die or attempt to...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78b73962f85c0980\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34e6f61e3ad19ead\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRailway safety statistics in the EU - Statistics Explained - Eurostat\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34e6f61e3ad19ead\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Railway_safety_statistics_in_the_EU\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"892aa5207092de12\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA total of 5 countries registered 4 or more deaths per thousand kilometres of railway tracks: <strong>Portugal (6.2), Hungary (5.8), Slovakia (5.7), Lithuania (4.6) and Poland (4.3).</strong> At the other end, 5 countries registered one or less fatality per thousand kilometres of railway tracks (Austria, Spain, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"892aa5207092de12\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ec.europa.eu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"126a624086d0429f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n(PDF) Suicide on the Railways in Belgium: A Typology of Locations and Potential for Prevention\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"126a624086d0429f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327803345_Suicide_on_the_Railways_in_Belgium_A_Typology_of_Locations_and_Potential_for_Prevention\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"90234bec1967c311\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStrale et al., 2018;Strauss et al., 2017). With respect to gender, most suicide by train attempts are by males, as is true for suicide overall (especially by violent methods) (Lukaschek et al., 2014;Wetzel, 2020).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"90234bec1967c311\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"2014\" \"2020\" railway suicide Eurostat Germany Belgium Portugal Spain France UK Croatia Bulgaria", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 898, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e75ddc976311c59\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n﻿ | I Report on Railway Safety and Interoperability in the EU 2020\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e75ddc976311c59\">>>", "url": "https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2022-10/Report%20on%20Railway%20Safety%20and%20Interoperability%20in%20the%20EU%202020.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2fa0c2ac947c788a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFigure A-20: Fatalities per type of accident (EU-28, 2014-18) Figure A-21: Railway suicide and trespasser fatalities (EU-28, 2007-18)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUS