{"type": "message", "id": "f20f3014", "parentId": "a8871b22", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T07:37:52.296Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Perfect! I have the data from Eurostat. Now I need to extract the 2014 and 2020 values for each of the mentioned countries: Germany (DE), Belgium (BE), Portugal (PT), Spain (ES), UK, France (FR), Croatia (HR), and Bulgaria (BG). Let me analyze the data:\n\nFrom the CSV data, I can see the railway suicide numbers (OBS_VALUE) for each country:\n\n**2014 values:**\n- Germany (DE): 781\n- Belgium (BE): 97  \n- Portugal (PT): 44\n- Spain (ES): 139\n- UK: 287\n- France (FR): 298\n- Croatia (HR): 28\n- Bulgaria (BG): 29\n\n**2020 values:**\n- Germany (DE): 678\n- Belgium (BE): 94\n- Portugal (PT): 23\n- Spain (ES): 69\n- UK: 251\n- France (FR): 203\n- Croatia (HR): 13\n- Bulgaria (BG): 20\n\nNow I need to calculate the percentage decrease for each country: ((2014 value - 2020 value) / 2014 value) × 100%\n\nLet me calculate:\n\n**Germany:** (781 - 678)/781 = 103/781 ≈ 13.2% decrease\n**Belgium:** (97 - 94)/97 = 3/97 ≈ 3.1% decrease  \n**Portugal:** (44 - 23)/44 = 21/44 ≈ 47.7% decrease\n**Spain:** (139 - 69)/139 = 70/139 ≈ 50.4% decrease\n**UK:** (287 - 251)/287 = 36/287 ≈ 12.5% decrease\n**France:** (298 - 203)/298 = 95/298 ≈ 31.9% decrease\n**Croatia:** (28 - 13)/28 = 15/28 ≈ 53.6% decrease\n**Bulgaria:** (29 - 20)/29 = 9/29 ≈ 31.0% decrease\n\nThe question asks: \"which of the following countries saw a decrease of less than 45% in suicides involving railways between the years of 2014 and 2020\"\n\nSo countries with less than 45% decrease: Germany (13.2%), Belgium (3.1%), UK (12.5%), France (31.9%), Bulgaria (31.0%)\n\nPortugal (47.7%), Spain (50.4%), and Croatia (53.6%) all have decreases greater than 45%.\n\nNow let me write the answer to the file:\n\n\n\n"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_6561ef257db54be7a2a9682a", "name": "write", "arguments": {"file": "answer.txt", "content": "Germany, Belgium,